WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.780
Australia toward the middle of 2021

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:07.870
was in a really difficult position

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:12.570
that A, eventually the
virus would find a way in,

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.640
and B, that Australia cannot be cut off

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.617
from the world indefinitely.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.044
We want freedom!

00:00:19.044 --> 00:00:20.650
We want freedom!

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.050
Such unprecedented shift

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:25.860
in how we live our lives was made

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.163
in face of this pandemic.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:32.510
This story was about the
really difficult transition

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.720
that Australia needed to pull off

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.650
in terms of figuring out how the country

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.490
was gonna move into the future

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:41.483
in a world where COVID
is just a part of life.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:52.230
So if you think back to February 2020,

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.973
things changed incredibly fast.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.380
We had a confirmation

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:59.950
of human to human transmission in Wuhan,

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:01.280
and then very quickly,

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.146
it's first case, first case, first case

00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:05.080
in just country after country,

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.163
all over the world.

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:12.070
In those critical weeks in Australia,

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:14.690
there weren't a lot of domestic measures

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:16.370
taken at that point.

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:19.140
There was no sign of the panic

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.940
that was then really just
starting to take hold

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:24.530
in parts of Europe and the United States.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:27.030
My name is Anika Stobart.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.700
I work at the Grattan Institute.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.530
which is Australia's
leading policy think tank.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:37.663
I work in the Health and
Aged Care Policy Program.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:43.480
A key contributor to the cases
in Australia's first wave

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:45.890
was the Ruby Princess cruise ship.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.530
People had been sick,

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:50.730
and these people didn't
actually end up in isolation.

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:53.070
They ended up back into the community.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:55.790
They contributed to a
lot of Australia's deaths

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:57.810
in that first wave.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.340
Australia was grappling with the idea

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:03.760
of how to manage the
COVID pandemic long term

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:07.660
when there weren't any
vaccines available at the time.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.050
And this is when this unique idea

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:13.050
of the COVID Zero approach emerged.

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:17.150
We are upgrading the
travel ban on Australians

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:19.720
to level four for the entire world.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:22.240
The travel advice to every Australian

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.909
is do not travel abroad.

00:02:24.909 --> 00:02:26.950
They just closed the borders completely.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:29.090
No one in and, and remarkably,

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.960
as the policy evolved it became clear

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.280
that the rule was no one out either.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:36.400
You needed to actually
apply for permission

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.570
from the Australian government

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:39.180
in order to leave the country.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.100
On the theory that anyone leaving

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.800
would eventually need to come back in,

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.200
and would thus be a
problem for the Australians

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.620
to keep COVID out.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:47.830
There was a lot of debate

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:51.100
about whether that was
the right way to do it.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.750
Essentially, there were two courses

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.960
that the state minister could take.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.510
One was to accept

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:59.110
that there would be a lot
of community transmission,

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:02.440
and therefore have to limbo
in and out of lockdowns

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:03.707
to control cases.

00:03:03.707 --> 00:03:05.220
And the alternative option

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.030
was to actually lockdown very strictly

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:10.810
in a way that enabled us to get to a point

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:14.090
where there were effectively zero cases.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:16.190
No tourists, no business travelers.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:18.310
The few people who were allowed to come in

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:21.084
spent 14 days in hotel quarantine,

00:03:21.084 --> 00:03:23.200
and it was enforced by the military.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.660
For anyone who breaches quarantine,

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.890
they face fines and even jail.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:32.683
The penalties ranging from
as much as $50,000 in WA

00:03:32.683 --> 00:03:34.360
and 12 months behind bars,

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:38.000
11,000 or six months
jail in New South Wales,

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.237
while Queensland, Victoria,
and South Australia

00:03:41.237 --> 00:03:43.240
all had the power to punish.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.840
These were devastating
public health measures

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:47.940
for many people.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:49.850
Australia is a nation of immigrants.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:53.200
Something like 30% of the
population was born abroad.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.130
So the inability to travel had huge costs,

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:59.050
personally, economically,
for many millions

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:01.433
of people in Australia and outside of it.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.540
It was difficult for people.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:06.740
Most Australians have connections

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:10.430
with communities
overseas, family, friends.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:13.830
Many businesses that relied
on international tourists

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:14.973
really struggled.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:20.970
But when the country emerged

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:22.860
from this first wave of lockdowns,

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.400
life, very rapidly

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:28.130
took on something like
its pre-COVID normalcy.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:30.468
You would go to bars and
beaches and restaurants.

00:04:30.468 --> 00:04:33.550
Hamilton even went on stage in Sydney.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:36.152
♪ I'm runnin' with the Sons of
Liberty and I am lovin' it ♪

00:04:36.152 --> 00:04:38.053
People were going into offices.

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:41.760
Because we are an island nation,

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:45.960
We had the opportunity to
actually have very few cases

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.280
in the community

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.003
until a vaccine would
hopefully arrive in the future.

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:55.100
Nationally, the daily case
numbers in some periods

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.260
were in the single or at
most the double digits.

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:01.360
They could go months
without a single COVID death

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.230
when the US, for example,

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:06.160
was recording literally
hundreds of thousands of deaths,

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.260
Australia might record
a death every few months

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:12.220
When Australia locked
down, they really did.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:15.080
They got the level down very, very low.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.473
We never really locked down as well

00:05:17.473 --> 00:05:19.770
or as completely as Australia did.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:23.740
So epidemiologically, in
terms of protecting lives,

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:27.313
these policies were spectacularly
successful in that period.

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:34.160
Once Australia was able
to return to normalcy

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.290
so much faster than the rest of the world,

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:38.460
you had overwhelming public support.

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:41.664
And so much so that anyone
who suggested an alternative

00:05:41.664 --> 00:05:43.510
was almost shouted down.

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:45.910
Virgin CEO has courted controversy

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.750
while calling for Australia's
international borders

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:50.770
to reopen before mid 2022.

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:53.530
At one point, the CEO of Virgin Australia

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:55.740
said eventually the
borders would have to open.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:58.440
And that when they do, people may die.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:02.000
Political figures
attacked her vociferously.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.020
Scott Morrison said he could have no truck

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:05.250
with comments like that.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:06.580
And it was a real warning

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:08.760
to other public figures in Australia,

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:12.474
that proposing to live
with the virus was a taboo.

00:06:12.474 --> 00:06:14.920
It was something you couldn't say.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:18.723
It became the third rail of
Australian politics for a time.

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:23.350
Whereas a lot of other countries,

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:25.120
the UK, Canada, the US,

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:28.690
moved to lockup vaccine
supplies as soon as they could,

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.370
Australia took a different approach

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:33.699
and a somewhat leisurely
one in retrospect.

00:06:33.699 --> 00:06:35.920
There was this kind of sense that,

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:37.520
from the government at least,

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.540
that things had been sorted.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:42.320
That there was this sense of complacency.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:45.040
And that kind of rolled
over into how they thought

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:46.720
about the vaccine rollout,

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:50.460
which was a key failure of
the government's response.

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:52.650
Australia didn't make a deal with Pfizer

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:54.490
until November 2020,

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:56.963
well after other countries had done so.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.470
Instead, Australia's strategy

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:02.260
was to focus on the AstraZeneca vaccine

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:04.533
through local manufacturing.

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:08.448
So when we started the vaccine roll out

00:07:08.448 --> 00:07:10.198
with the AstraZeneca,

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.720
we had couple of fatalities.

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:17.750
As the media highlighted fatality,

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.080
and inadvertently caused panic.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.900
I think the government,

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:23.880
they should have prepared the public

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.760
about those rare side effects.

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:26.900
And at the same time,

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:31.143
speeded up the Pfizer
MRNA-based vaccination.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:37.530
A major public education
campaign was underway.

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:39.949
visit Australia.gov.au.

00:07:39.949 --> 00:07:44.260
But it was mainly addressing
the mainstream Anglo-Saxon

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:46.780
background communities and society,

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:49.890
and they left the non-English
speaking community

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:52.130
through that public educations campaign.

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:56.080
And the weakest point for
the spread of that virus

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:00.220
was in people who were not targeted

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:03.680
by a public educations campaign.

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:06.130
I started in front of my house

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:09.097
a COVID assessment and testing clinic,

00:08:09.097 --> 00:08:11.320
and it was a drive-through.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:14.710
I used that also as an education area

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:17.080
where I can send the right messages

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:20.410
to our local community in the
Canterbury Bankstown area.

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:25.410
There was much influence of
pseudo science on social media

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:29.213
and a lot of propaganda
and conspiracy theories.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:35.920
The public did not have
the right information

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:39.800
about COVID pandemic and the virus itself.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:40.890
And unfortunately,

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:43.850
that gap needed to be addressed very soon.

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:49.470
A few months ago, Australia
was the envy of the world,

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:51.200
winning the war against COVID.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:53.380
Borders closed, but businesses open.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.370
Life, relatively normal.

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:58.510
But as the highly infectious
Delta variant takes hold

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:00.940
and our vaccine roll out lags,

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:04.620
we're becoming headline news
for all the wrong reasons.

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:07.830
Delta became the dominant strain,

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:10.120
and made its way to Australia

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:12.760
through leakages in hotel quarantine,

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:15.740
and ended up causing a major outbreak

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:19.490
In March, 2021, around 3% of Australians

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:20.970
had been fully vaccinated

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:24.340
whereas the US and UK
were well on their way

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:26.600
to vaccinating the bulk
of their populations.

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:28.470
A more transmissible variant

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:30.830
in an undervaccinated population

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:33.350
is kind of a nightmare scenario.

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:36.090
So Australia had to panic,

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:38.300
and that meant these very harsh lockdowns.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:41.030
And it also meant an effort
to step up vaccination

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:43.000
as quickly as they could.

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:46.020
It started in Australia's
most populous state,

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.260
New south Wales,

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:49.710
and then eventually spread to Victoria,

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:52.490
Australia's second most populous state.

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:55.200
Half the country was in lockdowns

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.320
Schools closed, offices closed,

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:01.830
all of these freedoms that
Australians had taken for granted

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:04.650
for the better part of the last year

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:06.910
were once again taken away.

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:10.160
All Australians need
to accept a hard truth.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:12.260
COVID is here to stay.

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:14.400
Delta was just too transmissible.

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:15.650
The genie was outta the bottle.

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:18.920
Australia was never gonna be
able to get back to COVID Zero.

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:21.900
Australia needed to come
to a new understanding

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:24.773
of what living in the
COVID age looked like.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:29.890
That today, it was
confirmed and fully agreed

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:32.250
that the national plan, that pathway,

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:35.220
that takes us to the position
where we live with this virus.

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:36.160
And we live with the virus

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:40.050
where we ultimately start
saying goodbye to lockdowns

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:43.570
once we reach 70%
vaccination of the population

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:46.200
This U-turn was politically controversial.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:47.750
There was a lot of criticism,

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.910
particularly Western
Australia and Queensland.

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:54.440
The premiers of those states
were not really on board.

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:56.073
Politics with a battle erupting

00:10:56.073 --> 00:10:58.870
over how the states manage the virus.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:02.965
Mark McGowan insists WA's
freedoms need to be maintained.

00:11:02.965 --> 00:11:05.430
We don't need rash decision making

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:08.780
on the basis of what is
occurring in New South Wales.

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:11.260
There is an Australia
outside of New south Wales.

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:12.620
Let's have a look at the number of cases

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:14.200
in New south Wales,

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:17.020
and Queenslanders don't
wanna see those cases numbers

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:17.970
coming to Queensland,

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:20.490
so that is why there is a border closure

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:22.120
But there was, I think,

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:23.610
a sense of resignation

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:25.360
that this was the only way to go.

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:28.680
This cycle of of lockdowns,
and freedom lockdowns,

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:30.240
and freedom had to stop.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:32.240
And that the only way to stop it

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:33.783
was to try a new approach.

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:39.470
Easing restrictions, but
only easing restrictions

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:42.950
for people that were double vaccinated.

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:45.480
People that were unvaccinated

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:46.940
would essentially continue

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:49.630
to have the lockdown restrictions

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:51.560
apply to them indefinitely.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:54.850
18 months of isolation and frustration

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:56.330
boils to breaking point.

00:11:58.180 --> 00:12:00.480
So-called freedom rally in Melbourne,

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:04.000
seeing violence break out
between protestors and police.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:08.000
Some people felt like
this was imposing on them

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:09.839
in a way that they didn't support.

00:12:09.839 --> 00:12:11.192
We want freedom!

00:12:11.192 --> 00:12:12.760
We want freedom!

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:16.170
There were some protests
against vaccine mandates

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:18.000
which got pretty ugly at times.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.020
Governments did not back down.

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:23.078
There was really very little
compromise at any point.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.260
You must be double vaccinated

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:27.430
in order to enter Australia,

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:29.200
with essentially no exceptions.

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:30.440
One example of that,

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:33.240
kind of spectacular example
of that was Novak Djokovic.

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:35.170
Arguably the best tennis
player in the world,

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:37.040
was kicked out of Australia

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:39.640
because he had entered without
being double vaccinated

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:41.470
to play in the Australian Open.

00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:43.450
Djokovic had his visa revoked

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:46.820
after being held at Melbourne
Airport for several hours.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:48.640
There should be no special rules

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:50.180
for Novak Djokovic at all.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:52.190
That is an example of just how serious

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:53.810
the Australian government is going to take

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:54.933
the vaccination issue.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:13:00.700
Once vaccination rates in
Australia reached high levels,

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:03.880
this triggered different
levels of liberalization.

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:05.920
We saw an end to lockdown measures.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:08.630
Things like restaurants
and nightclubs reopened.

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:12.180
In November, the borders
reopened in some respects.

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:14.270
The first flight from Los Angeles today

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.760
was QF12 under the new conditions.

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:18.300
And there was a real party mood down here

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:20.650
at Sydney Airport's arrivals terminal.

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:22.610
Omicron has come in and has arrived

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:25.050
with the same full force
that it did elsewhere,

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:27.369
but high vaccination
rates have done the job

00:13:27.369 --> 00:13:30.610
of preventing large numbers of deaths.

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:34.060
So I don't think there
are many strong arguments

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:37.070
against the policy mix
that Australia pursued.

00:13:37.070 --> 00:13:39.380
It saved an incredible number of lives.

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:42.040
Economically, it's a little less clear.

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:45.070
If you look at 2020 GDP
performance across major economies,

00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:47.020
Australia was more or less flat.

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:49.730
And part of that was simply being able

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:50.760
to get back to normal.

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:53.440
Resuming normal life for most people

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:57.940
most of the time was a a
bigger economic positive

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:00.440
than closing the borders
was an economic negative.

